mod-nats (0.5.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security hardening: fs.native.app refuses shell-exec apps (system,
    bg_system) with 403; fs.channel.setvar applies the same forbidden-
    variable filter as Dial (execute_on_*, api_on_*, api_hangup_hook,
    exec_after_*).
  * CHANNEL_DESTROY now drops the channel binding as a second chance after
    HANGUP_COMPLETE, so a dropped event cannot leak a claimed binding.
  * Inbound subscription drop counter (cnats pending limits) surfaced in
    `nats status` as `sub dropped`.
  * Docs state honestly that module-side TLS is not implemented.
  * Go SDK: caller context now reaches the wire request (ctx was silently
    ignored); all methods pass cancellation and deadlines through.
  * Wire catalog drift check (tests/check_catalog.py) runs in CI.

 -- lixuanqun <lixuanqun@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

mod-nats (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ownership lease with fs.channel.touch and Event.OwnerLost takeover.
  * fs.channel.record / XNode.Record session recordings.
  * Event.Detected: DTMF forwarding and layer-1 ASR results
    (fs.channel.detectspeech / XNode.DetectSpeech).
  * Idempotency keys for retry-safe control requests.
  * Leg operations: Transfer, Hold, Mute, ThreeWay, UnBridge2.
  * Go SDK under sdk/go.

 -- lixuanqun <lixuanqun@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 01 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

